OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G1/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FAre BBC channels heading for an early
OL,7,Fbath as the corporation strives to save
OL,8,Fmoney?
OL,10,FOn Saturday 1st August, the scheduled
OL,11,Fhandover to the BBC News Channel on BBC
OL,12,FOne was unusually early.
OL,14,FBBC One shut up shop at 12.05am.
OL,16,FIt's not the first time this has
OL,17,Fhappened this year.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G2/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn general, the handover during the
OL,7,Fweek seems to have crept forward
OL,8,Falthough there are still occasions when
OL,9,Fa clear effort is made to stay on the
OL,10,Fair late ` for example, late night
OL,11,Frepeats of The Hit List.
OL,13,FWould an early bath save much money
OL,14,Fthough?
OL,16,FGenerally, costs are incurred in the
OL,17,Fproduction of the programme ` or, in
OL,18,Fsome cases, with distinct repeat fees.
OL,20,FThe cost is not in the transmission as
OL,21,Fsuch.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14103
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G3/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe BBC's contract with Red Bee will
OL,7,Fallow for the potential for the main
OL,8,Fchannels to run well into the night.
OL,9,FIndeed there are occasions when they
OL,10,Fare 24-hour operations.
OL,12,FBut if you're trying to save money,
OL,13,Fevery little helps.
OL,15,FFor instance, dropping a late night
OL,16,Ffilm would give the BBC the opportunity
OL,17,Fto exercise its rights to show films
OL,18,Fmore sparingly.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14104
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G4/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FI hate to say this, but some
OL,7,Fcontraction around the margins of the
OL,8,Fschedule may help demonstrate the BBC's
OL,9,Ffinancial sutuation.
OL,11,FFor example, does BBC Two need to run
OL,12,Fdaytime repeats at 6.30am? Should both
OL,13,Fmain networks consistently finish
OL,14,Faround midnight on weekdays before
OL,15,Fjoining the News Channel or Sign Zone?
OL,17,FI wonder too about BBC Two's afternoon
OL,18,Fcollection of geriatric editions of
OL,19,Fquiz shows and Flog It. Would an
OL,20,Fafternoon News Channel simulcast be an
OL,21,Foption? Or would that just be too
OL,22,Fpainful for daytime viewers?
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14105
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G5/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs I say, the savings are marginal but
OL,7,Fthe symbolism of any such reductions in
OL,8,Foutput could be huge.
OL,10,FThe elephant in the room, of course, is
OL,11,Fthe long-term future of BBC Three and
OL,12,FBBC Four.
OL,14,FBoth are shadows of what they once
OL,15,Fwere.
OL,17,FThree has struggled to make an impact
OL,18,Fsince it was raised from the grave.
OL,20,FFour is principally a repeats and
OL,21,Farchive channel. Arguably this kind of
OL,22,Fcontent is better off on the iPlayer.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14106
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G6/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FHowever it is clearly appreciated by
OL,7,Fthose who don't have iPlayer access on
OL,8,Ftheir TVs and a linear schedule can
OL,9,Fstill be a good tool for raising
OL,10,Fawareness of the content.
OL,12,FI cannot imagine any marginal cuts will
OL,13,Fbe stealth cuts as such though.
OL,15,FIt's clear the BBC will be trying to
OL,16,Fdemonstrate that every axed programme
OL,17,Fand efficiency saving is a consequence
OL,18,Fof its financial position.
OL,20,FIt needs to exercise a little care in
OL,21,Fdoing this though.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14107
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G7/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FHad Blankety Blank and the like simply
OL,7,Fcome to the end?
OL,9,FIf so, the saving is in the decision
OL,10,Fnot to replace it and cut the total
OL,11,Famount of commissioned content.
OL,13,FIf it simply was a cut, the implication
OL,14,Fis that the show will return if the
OL,15,Ffinancial situation eases.
OL,17,FThose with long memories will recall
OL,18,Fthe dramatic cuts of 1975.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14108
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G8/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe TV savings were principally made by
OL,7,Fcutting output then seen as marginal
OL,8,Fsuch as the half hearted effort to
OL,9,Fcompete with ITV's full afternoon
OL,10,Fschedule.
OL,12,FI'd rather see these symbolic cuts than
OL,13,Fan increase in repeats, imports or
OL,14,Fcheaper programmes.
OL,16,FBut genuine efficiency savings are
OL,17,Fnever a bad thing.
OL,19,FIf the weather can be more cost
OL,20,Feffective, I have no problem though I
OL,21,Fdo think some of the detailed proposals
OL,22,Fdo need debated.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14109
SC,0009
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G9/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FYet again it all boils down to a few
OL,7,Fbasics.
OL,9,F- Is the BBC stretching itself too
OL,10,Fthinly?
OL,12,F- Would contracting services help it
OL,13,Fspend its money more wisely? Or mean
OL,14,Fthat some people were not being
OL,15,Fadequately served?
OL,17,F- And, of course, the fundamental
OL,18,Ffunding situation needs to be very high
OL,19,Fon the political radar.
OL,21,FSoon after the 1975 cuts, the BBC got a
OL,22,Fsignificant licence fee rise.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14110
SC,0010
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1785674492
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}        G10/10
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCLast orders at midnight: the
OL,4,Cquiet contraction of BBC schedules
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt wasn't the rise the corporation
OL,7,Fwanted ` the black and white rise
OL,8,Fwasn't so big and at this time more
OL,9,Fthan half of households still had
OL,10,Fmonochrome sets.
OL,12,FI am sure this was spun as the
OL,13,Fgovernment helping a key public service
OL,14,Fwhile remaining mindful of the pressure
OL,15,Fon those struggling with the cost of
OL,16,Fliving. Familiar?
OL,18,FThe 1975 increase didn't reverse the
OL,19,Fcuts. But it did prevent much more
OL,20,Fhorrible decisions from taking place.
OL,23,EPub: 02-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
